WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.438
ALEX: On announcement day. Which is
different from in production.

00:00:04.548 --> 00:00:08.882
RUFUS: A vendor claim about scale and
safety is not independent validation.
NVIDIA

00:00:08.882 --> 00:00:13.215
RUFUS: says this. The partners say
they're integrating. Whether it works as
described

00:00:13.215 --> 00:00:17.549
RUFUS: in a live enterprise environment
is a separate question.

00:00:17.729 --> 00:00:21.983
JAMIE: And that's the real continuity
here — yesterday we had an unresolved

00:00:21.983 --> 00:00:26.237
JAMIE: argument about whether this would
be a genuine security advance or
expensive

00:00:26.237 --> 00:00:30.491
JAMIE: AI bureaucracy. Now we have the
actual product.

00:00:30.601 --> 00:00:33.803
ALEX: We do. And honestly, it moves the
needle. Not because it solves

00:00:33.803 --> 00:00:37.005
ALEX: the problem — it doesn't — but
because doing governance at the

00:00:37.005 --> 00:00:40.208
ALEX: hardware layer with identity
verification is more than most
enterprises have right

00:00:40.208 --> 00:00:43.410
ALEX: now.
